  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training basics of associations and cooperatives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chad is suffering of poor economic development, high rate of poverty and geo-political instability. Government services on basic development remain limited or nearly in-absent. Supporting informal and formal farmer groups based on social cohesion and principles of self-help, therefore makes sense. These associations can play an important role in local rural economic development.This project trains associations and farmer groups involved in ongoing LAND-at-scale and AgriJobBooster projects. It is planned to train and assist farmers&apos; groups to strengthen their organization and to discuss and define the objectives of (forming) the association or cooperative.Basically, two key questions will be addressed:1.	Why do we work together?2.	How do we work together?These key questions are discussed by addressing the basic principles of a cooperative, service provision to members, governance, and financial management.</narrative>
  </description>
